/**
 * DSH session transcript access.
 *
 * A DSH session is persisted as one zstd-compressed JSONL file:
 *   ~/.dsh/sessions/<workspace-slug>/<session-id>/session.v4.jsonl.zstd
 *
 * Line 0 is the session header ({"type":"session","version":4,"id":...,"cwd":...}).
 * Every later line is one recorded session event:
 *   {"type":"turn/start","seq":N,"time":<ms>,"data":{...}}
 *
 * Entire wants a plain transcript it can seek into by byte offset, so
 * prepare-transcript materializes the decompressed JSONL next to the original
 * and every analyzer call reads that file.
